SM(464,{"n":"Acts 11-12","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 11-12.mp3","d":2627.3,"s":[[0.4,"Come and study Holy Scripture with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.48,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed tradition, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.36,"And these days prophets came from Jerusalem to Antioch."],[24.8,"And one of them, named Agabas, stood up and showed by the Spirit that there was going to be a great famine throughout all the world, which also happened in the days of Claudius Caesar."],[38.56,"I mean, this is sort of out of the blue."],[40.64,"It sounds like suddenly we're in the Old Testament."],[45.76,"Well, we have to understand uh what's meant by prophet."],[53.32,"Uh and part of the part of the problem is our modern use of the word prophet is not the same as the Old Testament use of the word prophet."],[59.84,"The Hebrew word is Navi"],[64.68,"Uh it's that we get profit from profitis in in uh Greek."],[69.64,"The Greek word that's used for it."],[71.56,"Um we tend to think when we say prophet, we mean somebody who predicts the future."],[76.44,"Uh-huh. And that's not what it meant in the Old Testament."],[80.65,"Uh some of the things that the prophets say are talking about the future."],[85.45,"But some of the things are not about the future."],[87.21,"Some of them are about the present, some of them are about the past."],[90.3,"Um a a prophet in in this and and the word is used, of course, by pagan Greeks."],[98.46,"The word is used, word Navi in in Hebrew and Aramaic is used by pagans in the ancient Near East."],[108.34,"Yeah, they're false prophets of the Old Testament."],[109.94,"There are prop, you know, Balaam, the son of Baor, is a prophet of one of the Canaanite gods in the Old Testament."],[116.82,"And a prophet was a representative, it was someone who had been called by God or a god, claimed to be a god."],[128.71,"Um, and who came uh with a message from that god for a particular purpose."],[138.87,"Um what went with that was a certain lifestyle."],[146.15,"Um we read in in 1st and 2nd Kings or 3rd and 4th Kingdoms the Septuagint that there were whole communities of prophets."],[162.27,"And so, of course, sort of the sin qua non of the prophets is Saint Elias, the prophet Elijah in the Old Testament, and similarly St."],[175.15,"John the Forerunner, Saint John the Baptist, in the in the New Testament, who are called to this particular lifestyle and who are given this message."],[183.09,"But we talked about in in chapter 9 that uh Saint Paul on the road to Damascus, when he has this vision, the language that's used there is all drawn from places where the prophets were called in the Old Testament."],[198.35,"When when Isaiah's ministry begins, he has this vision of God enthroned in the temple with the altar as his footstool."],[207.15,"He sort of sees God and God, you know, sends him with this message."],[213.07,"Um the uh prophet Jeremiah, uh, God says to him that he formed him in his mother's womb, uh, which is language that St."],[224.19,"Paul's gonna pick up on in Galatians, that God had called him from his mother's womb."],[229.07,"He says to Jeremiah that he formed him uh called him from his mother's womb uh to be a uh prophet to the nations."],[236.91,"Of course, in Greek, that's you know, prophet to the Gentiles"],[237.19,"That's how it's usually translated into English."],[244.72,"And St. Paul says in Galatian that he was called, God had called him from his mother's womb to be the apostle to the Gentiles."],[252.98,"And so there's some some crossover there too."],[256.82,"So these prophets are people who God has given this commission to go and do or go and say something."],[265.94,"And what they're doing is the prophets, what the prophets did in the Old Testament was they didn't just preach anything."],[271.86,"It wasn't just God, I'm gonna give out some info."],[275.59,"Here's your lucky lotto numbers for next week, or you know, here's the you know don't plant on this side of the Jordan because it's gonna flood."],[283.53,"It wasn't stuff like that."],[284.89,"It was very specific stuff for a specific reason."],[288.09,"And and it was primarily uh repeating and calling the people back to the Torah."],[296.67,"The teaching of God that He'd already revealed."],[298.93,"So the prophet would come and say, Look, you are disobedient."],[302.79,"You are doing this and this and this and this, and these are all the things that God commanded you not to do."],[307.67,"And if you do not repent, judgment is gonna come and befall you, and you' greonna or if judgment had already come and befall befallen them, it would be, you know, you guys, the reason this judgment befell you is because you did X, Y, Z."],[322.55,"But now, if you turn back and you repent, God will bless you and He will restore you."],[327.24,"Now that's talking about things that are going to happen in the future."],[330.14,"But the focus is not just predicting the future."],[333.26,"It's saying this is gonna what is going to happen if you don't follow God or if you turn back to God, these good things, which is what you find at the end of the book of Deuteronomy."],[347.42,"At the end of the Torah, the last book of the Pentateuch, in Deuteronomy, chapters 28 through 30, God says, Today I set before you life and death, blessings and curses."],[358.5,"Choose. If you live this way and do these things, I will bless you."],[363.52,"If you live this way and do these things, you'll be accursed, and this is what will happen to you."],[368.5,"And then he even goes so far as to say, and once you've done all these things that I've cursed you."],[373.72,"And I've thrown you out of the land."],[375.32,"If you turn back, then I will still blend you."],[379.57,"Because he knew it was what was going to happen."],[382.42,"And so that's that's at its core what the message of the prophets always was was calling them back to that."],[389.78,"Say, remember when God said to you."],[392.39,"You've been choosing death."],[394.57,"You need to choose life."],[396.89,"You need to choose blessings."],[398.89,"So uh this phenomenon doesn't just sort of immediately stop."],[406.51,"And in fact, the preaching ministry of the church in general is a continuation of that prophetic word."],[417.67,"That's why we call it a homily."],[420.55,"Because a homily means the same."],[423.8,"Almost the same."],[425.88,"So if I'm doing what I'm supposed to be doing when I preach a homily, it's saying the same thing that the scriptures said."],[434.2,"It's supposed to be calling the people back to look, come back to this."],[438.04,"This is what scriptures say."],[440.04,"I don't know that."],[441.32,"Yeah. Come back to this."],[443.82,"So really the whole preaching ministry is a continuation of that."],[448.42,"So these and these are Christians from the Christian community."],[452.38,"the Christian. Jewish Christians who are going now to Jewish community"],[460.48,"And so that's part of why their ministry is understood in these prophetic terms."],[467.25,"Because it's within this Jewish context."],[472.69,"So St. Paul, St."],[474.29,"Barnabas, they've been preaching to this nascent Gentile Christian community."],[481.33,"These prophets are coming to the Jewish Christian community who understand their preaching and their teaching within this context of prophecy."],[494.77,"Whereas the Gentiles wouldn't have necessarily understood it in the same way."],[504.73,"And so we're going to see that one of them in particular has a message for that."],[511.61,"And that that was Agabas."],[513.29,"Agabus is going to show up later."],[515.53,"This isn't the last we'll see of St."],[517.93,"Agabus. He got up and he talks about the fact that there is this famine coming."],[528.53,"Uh and that this happened that it actually happened."],[532.41,"The famine It says also happened, which is kind of confusing."],[537.53,"Like he talked about one famine, and there was another famine?"],[540.33,"No, but he's the famine's he. talking about happened in the days of Claudius"],[544.69,"So this is one of the we don't get a lot of temporal markers in terms of how much time has passed."],[550.61,"Right as we go through."],[552.53,"But if this is if this is the reign of Claudius, we're now in the forties."],[560.53,"So we we talked about so a fair amount of time has passed since we talked about the the conversion of uh St."],[570.61,"Paul. Again, we're using the word conversion just for simplicity's sake, even though we talked about um St."],[576.53,"Paul's calling, the road to Damascus happened in in about 35."],[581.33,"Around 35. And so a considerable number of years have passed now. as we get this temporal marker that we're now in the reign of Claudius"],[593.85,"Then the disciples, each according to his bid ability, determined to send relief to the brethren dwelling in Judea."],[600.57,"This they also did and sent it to the elders in the hands of Barnabas and Saul."],[607.13,"So because there's going to be this famine, they sort of take a collection."],[614.75,"And send that money back to uh the uh the Jerusalem community."],[622.03,"This is important for a few reasons."],[624.51,"Um not just because as we mentioned, the Jewish community in in Antioch is large. and well established and wealthier on the whole than most of the Jews in Judea"],[637.99,"Because remember, in Judea, 70% of the land that's not owned by Rome is owned by the high priests and their family."],[652.63,"There's been this economic oppression by the Sadducees and the chief priests and the religious leaders in Judea, but not many of those folks have come to follow Jesus Christ"],[668.87,"Meaning the Christian community there is not from this sort of landed class."],[674.71,"There are people like St."],[676.99,"Peter, St. John, you know, fishermen, tradesmen."],[680.69,"And so uh Antioch, the the this Jewish community in Antioch has that's been thriving and has been established there for a long time is wealthier."],[690.37,"And so they share with this other community."],[693.89,"Um but this also shows us, this also shows us that you know, notice it's referred to as the brethren in Judea."],[705.01,"Meaning already at this point, we're in the 40s."],[708.59,"They already have this understanding that uh it's not, okay, well, there's this church here and there's this church here, and we get along with it, but that they're part of one family across this geographic distance."],[729.43,"And this is going to this is going to continue, as we're going to see as we go forward."],[735.45,"Um, that uh they aren't sort of congregationalists."],[740.59,"They aren't sort of this is our group, and we're gonna govern our group, and you do your group, and this, but they they see themselves as one family."],[747.63,"They're helping each other financially."],[750.43,"Teachers are going back and forth from one to the other to build them up."],[753.95,"They're all part of one body, even though they're spread out."],[757.07,"They're spread out in these different places."],[759.23,"And that's a shift."],[761.19,"Because there were synagogues in all of these places."],[765.03,"But this is not the way that the Jewish communities understood themselves."],[769.12,"Because remember, the Jewish communities were all centered around the temple."],[772.56,"Temple of Jerusalem is where all the sacrifices take place."],[776.4,"That's where all the action is."],[778.34,"In terms of the pre existing Jewish religion."],[782.18,"That's where the rituals are."],[784.1,"The synagogues are just sort of gathering places for us as Jewish people to get together and pray since we can't get to Jerusalem that often because we live in Rome, or we live in Cyrene, or we live in, you know, at this great distance."],[799.14,"That's not the way, however, that these churches are viewing themselves."],[804.9,"They're not viewing the Jerusalem church as, well, this is. where everything's happening"],[810.06,"This is the King Church, and you know."],[812.51,"But that the Church of Christ."],[815.57,"Remember, Christ, as St."],[817.33,"Barnabas said, is there with them in Antioch."],[820.61,"And he's there with them in Jerusalem."],[823.43,"That the church is one body that's spread out all over the."],[829.03,"And the reason I'm making such an issue of this is that there are a whole bunch of scholars who are gonna say that, for example, because 1st and Second Timothy and Titus talk about, and Ephesians talk about the church, the church, as this one big Well, those St."],[846.63,"Paul can't have written those because they didn't come up with that idea until long after St."],[851.03,"Paul was dead."],[855.08,"They were all these separate communities and they all did things differently, and they all right."],[859.8,"But that's not."],[861.64,"I mean, we're here in Acts."],[863.42,"We're here in the 40s."],[864.7,"And that's not how they understand themselves."],[867.18,"They already understand themselves as this one family, as this one body."],[872.7,"Well, this action that they take seems to be a joint action of the Jewish Christians and the Hellenist Christians."],[881.18,"It's this bonding them together more than they were before."],[885.26,"One would hope."],[886.46,"Yeah. We're gonna find out that there are still some tensions there."],[889.34,"Uh huh. Both here in Acts and even more so, it's gonna get talked about in Galatians."],[893.58,"Uh-huh. Uh, some things that happen."],[895.1,"So there are, but sending the collection with Barnabas and Saul, I think, is an attempt to try to present a united."],[904.58,"And also to send Barnabas and Saul back to Jerusalem in order that they can tell the community of Jerusalem about the wonderful things that are going on, you know, have been going on over the last year, uh-huh, you know, in in Antioch."],[922.44,"But they have Jerusalem and Antioch have this at this point close close relationship."],[928.68,"They consider themselves to be part of this one family, not as two separate geographic units uh the yes shame of shame of us to be we've run one money not one church thousands of church yeah essentially yeah yeah and Jesus wants us left one church I think I'm actually much so um yeah it's uh it's a well we'll we'll we'll see what happens."],[973.78,"We'll talk about that more when we when we get into Galatians and see what's going on in Antioch."],[979.32,"And and all the work that St."],[985.64,"Paul does to try to make sure that we don't end up with two different with a Gentile church and a Jewish church."],[992.6,"You know, which he does not want."],[995.88,"That that because that in and of itself is sort of a betrayal of the gospel."],[1002.05,"That Jesus is Lord of everyone."],[1004.79,"And what he's done."],[1006.31,"And it's going to take a lot of effort because the two are gonna, even though here we see them trying to put forward this united Front, there are going to be those tensions and they are gonna start to uh pull apart from each other over a few different issues."],[1027.51,"I think we can go on a a little bit a little bit further, even though we're at the end of chapter."],[1034.43,"Chapter 12, verse 1."],[1036.03,"Now, about that time Herod the king stretched out his hand to harass some from the church."],[1043.47,"So this isn't the same, you know, we've had a couple of Herods."],[1050.75,"There was uh and uh an original Herod."],[1055.25,"The Herod who who killed the infants at the time of Jesus' birth in St."],[1059.65,"Matthew's gospel was Herod the Great."],[1062.45,"Um who was the original Herod."],[1065.17,"Uh who was not Jewish."],[1067.65,"Uh he was he was Idumean, uh which means he was at that time the Jews would have considered him an Edomite."],[1072.69,"he was. By our modern terminology, an Arab"],[1079.45,"He was from one of the tribes, the desert tribes."],[1084.09,"He was by all accounts a really good politician."],[1088.97,"That's sort of how he weasel his way into the Romans, making him the king."],[1096.17,"Now that title, he was sort of like the king of England today, or the queen of England today, as we currently have."],[1103.05,"That's like the English word."],[1104.73,"Where they don't have a ton of actual power, you know, in terms of government."],[1111.37,"His official title from the Romans was Ethnarch, which meant king of the people."],[1117.61,"And the reason they called him King of the People is uh the Jewish people weren't Roman citizens, so the Romans basically didn't care about them."],[1126.61,"Uh the Romans cared about the land, the natural resources, the roads they could use for trade."],[1133.01,"Those are the things they cared about."],[1134.85,"And so the people who happened to be living living there were sort of like the animals that might happen to be living there."],[1140.53,"You know, they kind of got in the way a lot, but they were useful for slave labor."],[1145.09,"You know, so it was sort of a toss up."],[1148.05,"And so them making him king of the people was not really a lofty title."],[1154.29,"Um basically, he was very wealthy, sort of like the modern day British monarchy, couldn't really do much."],[1161.73,"Um the Romans expected once in a while would call on him to try and keep the people in line."],[1163.25,"He was sort of a figurehead"],[1173.13,"That said, he he had a uh he had a fascinating career, including at one point trying to romance Cleopatra in order to jockey for position."],[1184.89,"Um he ended up he he switched allegiances in the Civil War between Mark Antony and and Octavian, who later became Caesar Augustus."],[1193.53,"He was involved in all the politics of his day."],[1195.85,"Um and the Romans weren't very happy with him at the time he died."],[1200.01,"And so uh because they were unhappy with him at the time he died, they split his already his quote-unquote territory. which you know was sort of he was sort of a figurehead, they split it in four and gave each of his four sons one piece"],[1215.89,"That's why uh his son is off, and this is his son, Herod, is often referred to as Herod the Tetrarch, which means ruler of a fourth."],[1225.3,"So he only had a quarter of the you know lack of power and you know modest wealth of his father."],[1233.54,"Um his father, the main thing he had done was huge building projects like the temple that was worked on for 40 years, that he turned into the huge temple complex."],[1244.34,"Uh but he built a number of other things too."],[1246.34,"A lot of them were Roman buildings."],[1247.7,"He built baths and theaters and this kind of thing."],[1252.06,"He built a lot of fortresses and palaces."],[1257.34,"That kind of thing."],[1258.22,"And he was, by those standards, he was sort of a great artist."],[1260.7,"He made a lot of uh, I'm not going to go too much into this, but if you're interested in ancient architecture, you can find a lot about Herod's building projects."],[1268.38,"He innovated in a few things in terms of Roman design and then was copied by other people."],[1277.34,"But so this is his son."],[1278.86,"This is not Herod the Great."],[1280.46,"This is Herod the not so great."],[1283.34,"This is his son, who is the one who tried to put Jesus on trial."],[1292.7,"Not that he could really do anything about it, but that was one of the attempts by Pilate. to sort of say, don't bother me with this"],[1300.1,"You know, take him to Herod, let Herod deal with him."],[1302.68,"I don't have time for this kind of thing."],[1305.8,"Um so this is that same Herod, and now he's decided he's he's causing some trouble, for the uh Christian community in Jerusalem."],[1317.04,"Then he killed James, the brother of John with the sword."],[1320.48,"Okay, so Saint this is not the Saint James, the not Saint James, the brother of the Lord, not Jesus' brother James, his foster brother James, uh, who uh we're gonna see is gonna continue to be a leader in the Church of Jerusalem."],[1338.16,"Yeah, he was Saint Joseph's son, St."],[1341.16,"Sa Jintames, the brother of the Lord."],[1341.52,"So not him"],[1342.68,"Yeah. He's this is this is Saint James, son of Zebedee."],[1351.4,"Saint John's brother."],[1354.28,"So in the Gospels, we saw sort of Jesus' inner circle of three disciples were Saints Peter, James, and John."],[1361.4,"This is that James."],[1362.92,"He's the first of he's the first of the apostles, the first of the disciples to be martyred."],[1368.12,"So when they refer to St."],[1369.56,"James the Great, this is what they mean, or did they mean the brother of the children?"],[1373.48,"This is usually Saint James, the son of Zebedee."],[1374.84,"of Zebedee. Son"],[1376.74,"And Saint James the lesser is Saint James the son of Alpheus, who is another one of the twelve."],[1381.3,"Okay. And then Saint James, the brother of the Lord, is a third person."],[1386.34,"He was not one of the twelve"],[1387.82,"Who is Santiago?"],[1390.46,"Iago is just the Spanish form of in Santiago."],[1396.78,"Yeah, I'm not sure."],[1397.58,"Santiago Chile, I'm not sure which."],[1400.14,"My guess would be Saint James the brother of the Lord, but I'm not totally sure."],[1403.5,"Uh-huh. That would be my guess."],[1407.34,"Um. And th the reason for that, the reason there's so many Jameses is the name in English James is translating Yaakovos, which is Jacob."],[1418.78,"So you could you could imagine there are a lot of Jewish people named Jacob."],[1423.5,"That's a very common, Jacob is a very common Jewish men's name."],[1427.9,"So that's why there's so many."],[1430.06,"Uh that we're running into."],[1431.26,"James's son of Zebedee here is killed by by Herod"],[1431.78,"But so this St."],[1436.74,"And old James was in uh Jesus' uh Titan."],[1442.1,"Mm-hmm. Yeah. Yeah."],[1447.14,"Yeah. And because he saw that it pleased the Jews, he proceeded further to seize Peter also."],[1457.22,"That was during the days of unleavened bread."],[1460.34,"Okay, so the feast of unleavened bread is the week leading up to the Passover."],[1468.18,"So he puts St."],[1470.02,"James to death."],[1470.9,"The Jews he's talking about."],[1473.22,"It's not just talking about just general, it's talking about. the Jewish leaders in Jerusalem"],[1479.56,"The Jewish authorities of Jerusalem, who, as we saw, were already not fond of the Christian community."],[1485.88,"And they had been they had been using sort of mob violence."],[1489.98,"Like with St."],[1490.62,"Stephen to get him stoned to death because they didn't have the authority to execute anybody."],[1494.46,"Well, Herod can get away with executing people, as we saw with St."],[1497.98,"John the Baptist."],[1500.06,"He could get away with executing people."],[1502.14,"And so he executes St."],[1504.06,"James. He sees that, oh hey, you know, and remember, the he he has no actual power."],[1511.18,"So the only power he has is based on popularity."],[1514.32,"The only influence he has is so, oh, hey, they're real happy."],[1518.48,"Well, I'll kill another one."],[1519.84,"So he has St."],[1520.32,"Peter arrested So when he had arrested him, he put him in prison and delivered him to four squads of soldiers to keep him, intending to bring him before the people after Passover."],[1537.48,"So again, he's got to be, even though he's not really Jewish, he's got to be sensitive."],[1542.13,"Remember, the whole point of this is to make him popular."],[1544.21,"Well, if he starts executing people during Passover, that's not going to go over all that well."],[1550.13,"The whole Aaron family tries to be as Jewish as they possibly can."],[1555.97,"That's part of their Yeah, but they're kind of faking it, and the Jews like to remind them that they're faking it."],[1561.81,"Yeah. ah. And so ye, he's not going to do that"],[1566.81,"So he's he has it, say Peter locked away."],[1570.19,"And locked away."],[1571.47,"The significance of it being four squads of soldiers is they've got him locked up in the garrison."],[1576.76,"Secure as you can get him."],[1578.5,"If someone's gonna break in and free him, they're gonna have to get past the whole military garrison."],[1584.76,"In order to get him out."],[1586.04,"And he's gonna keep it there, and then after the Passover and everything's over, he'll have bring him out and execute him to get some more praise from the Jewish authorities."],[1596.76,"Peter was therefore kept in prison, but constant prayer was offered to God for him by the church."],[1602.32,"Okay, so the community is praying for him."],[1606.68,"And when Herod was about to bring him out that night, Peter was sleeping, bound with two chains between two soldiers, and the guards before the door were keeping the prison."],[1617.36,"Okay. So they not only have him in the garrison, just to make sure he doesn't get away."],[1622.97,"Because remember, remember the last time they were arrested by the Jewish authorities."],[1628.25,"Remember the Saints Peter and John?"],[1630.81,"They're arrested by the authorities, and sort of the next thing they knew, they were out preaching again."],[1637.05,"So Herod's making very sure."],[1639.07,"He's not going anyplace."],[1640.59,"So they not only have him there, they not only have him chained up, but he's got one arm chained to one soldier."],[1646.03,"He's got the other arm chained to another soldier."],[1648.51,"Okay We're sitting there, and they got two more soldiers. at the door right into the room"],[1655.43,"So he's not going any place this time, as far as they're concerned."],[1660.47,"Now, behold, an angel of the Lord stood by him, and a light shone in the prison, and he struck Peter on the side and raised him up, saying, Arise quickly, and his chains fell off his hands."],[1675.35,"So presumably he was probably sleeping."],[1678.79,"So the angel kind of whacks him in the side to wake him up."],[1683.75,"Um and tells him, you know, get up, and the chains fall off."],[1692.43,"And the angel said to him, gird yourself and tie on your sandals."],[1697.55,"And so he did."],[1698.51,"And he said to him, Put on your garments and follow me."],[1701.23,"Now that gird yourself, I don't know if you've seen, there's actually a little diagram going around on online about what it means to gird up your loins."],[1709.63,"That's the phrase the King James used."],[1711.63,"Gird up your loins."],[1713.31,"And essentially, what it was was you have to remember, people are wearing robes."],[1718.93,"And so you would take basically the base of the robe and sort of tuck it up between your legs and then tuck it into your belt."],[1726.45,"more like shorts. And that would allow you to move"],[1732.01,"And efficiently. He's saying, come on, get up, get ready, let's go"],[1732.77,"So that's what he's saying."],[1740.53,"So he went out and followed him and did not know that what was done by the angel was real, but thought he was seeing a vision."],[1747.58,"So he doesn't know, you know, this happens all of a sudden."],[1750.94,"He was asleep."],[1751.92,"He doesn't am I asleep?"],[1753.6,"This is a dream or a vision for God or something."],[1756.56,"Or when they were past the first and the second guard posts."],[1762.18,"He's all the way back in the garrison."],[1764.18,"So he's got a the second guard post."],[1768.98,"They came to the iron gate that leads to the city, which opened to them of its own accord."],[1774.4,"So just like the chains just fell off, the gate into the city opens up."],[1779.6,"And they went out and went down one street, and immediately the angel departed from it."],[1783.92,"So now he's free and out on the streets of Jerusalem"],[1792.44,"And when Peter had come to himself, he sort of figures out what had happened."],[1799.0,"He said, Now I know for certain that the Lord has sent his angel and has delivered me from the hand of Herod and from all the expectation of the Jewish people."],[1806.76,"I like that translation the expectation of the Jewish people."],[1810.04,"What they were expecting was a public execution."],[1815.77,"So when he had considered this, he came to the house of Mary, the mother of John, whose surname was Mark, where many were gathered together praying."],[1824.49,"So this is we're now being introduced to another person."],[1827.85,"And again they use the word surname"],[1829.09,"Okay. Which is that there's a person named John."],[1836.61,"John is is the English John is derived from the Hebrew Jonah, which is again why that's a common name."],[1845.73,"And it's not a surname."],[1849.01,"It would actually be Marcus, which is a Latin Roman name."],[1853.49,"As we mentioned with with uh Saul, St."],[1857.89,"Paul, uh Jews who conducted a lot of business, or had some standing in the in the uh Roman world, or doing business in Greek, the the Romans weren't real great on pronouncing Jewish names correctly and didn't understand them or know what they meant."],[1883.24,"And so they would often take they would often take uh either Greek or Latin names to use when they were when they were doing business."],[1895.24,"This happens today."],[1896.52,"A lot of of uh Asian people I know who come to the United States, for example, because people in the United States have so much trouble pronouncing a lot of Asian names, will you know, they'll have an Asian name and then they'll have something that's kind of similar."],[1914.84,"They'll say, you know, people call me Peter, you know, or people call me, you know, people call me Mike, you know, or whatever."],[1917.64,"Like if your name is Bulos, you go by Paul"],[1921.76,"That's sort of similar."],[1925.78,"Um, so that's a similar thing."],[1928.34,"So the same thing was true then."],[1930.83,"None of these Greeks or Romans spoke any Aramaic."],[1935.47,"Didn't know how to pronounce all the a lot of the sounds like shh and stuff they didn't have, you know."],[1941.23,"So they would just use have a name they use."],[1943.63,"So this is it's not a surname, even though he's referred to sometimes as John Mark, that's not his last name."],[1950.11,"They didn't have last names."],[1951.47,"That's Marcus is the name that he went by when doing those things."],[1955.55,"And his mother's name was Mary."],[1957.63,"Mary, of course, comes from Miriam, who is Moses' sister, so that's a very popular Jewish name for women."],[1966.23,"Um, but so this is a house, uh the fact that it's her house implies that they had some money."],[1974.57,"Because for her to have a house, that would have to mean that her husband actually had this house in Jerusalem and had died and sort of left it to her."],[1984.01,"Um and so uh this is apparently, as we're gonna see, a a meeting place uh for the Christian community there."],[1991.53,"Because as we see, many were gathered there praying for Saint Peter."],[1996.33,"So this is probably one of the larger houses."],[1998.89,"This is probably one of the more well to do members of the Christian communities."],[2003.29,"Traditionally that would make sense too, because he's doing business with the larger world, and that's why he has this name."],[2013.26,"And this Saint John Mark is the Saint Mark who wrote the gospel of St."],[2020.06,"Mark. This is the Mark."],[2021.82,"This is him."],[2022.94,"This is him."],[2023.74,"He's going to we're he's gonna show up later on too."],[2026.22,"Okay. And he's gonna uh work with Saint Paul and then later with Saint Peter."],[2031.66,"Yes. And uh it's under and he's going to his gospel is gonna be recording uh Saint Peter's preaching, since he was a companion of Saint Peter's in Rome."],[2042.3,"He's going to from St."],[2043.58,"Peter's preaching write his write his gospel."],[2047.66,"But that's who this is. is, who still a very young man at this point"],[2054.74,"But so Saint Peter sort of figures out where he is and what's going on."],[2060.02,"He's actually awake and he's actually free."],[2062.1,"And so he heads over to this place, this house where they meet, where uh they're meeting currently and praying for him to be freed."],[2069.62,"And as Peter knocked on the door of the gate, a girl named Rhoda came to answer."],[2075.38,"So this is a servant girl in the household."],[2079.3,"When she recognized Peter's voice, because of her gladness, she did not open the gate, but ran in and announced that Peter stood before the gate."],[2088.74,"So she goes and she peeks out and sees that it's St."],[2091.78,"Peter. She gets so excited."],[2093.46,"He's out of prison."],[2093.86,"of And instead letting him in, runs back into, hey everybody!"],[2099.82,"St. Peter's at the door."],[2105.18,"But they said to her, You are beside yourself."],[2108.46,"That's a nice translation, too."],[2110.06,"Basically, they said, You're crazy."],[2112.52,"What do you mean he's standing at the door?"],[2114.04,"He's in prison."],[2114.76,"They're gonna execute him tomorrow."],[2119.89,"Yet she kept insisting that it was so."],[2122.37,"So they said, It is his angel."],[2125.91,"So they say, Oh, he must have, he must have died already."],[2130.15,"They must have already, they must have executed him early, and this is his spirit."],[2135.83,"Now Peter continued knocking"],[2142.83,"Meanwhile, Saint Peter, while they're having this discussion, he's still standing out there in the middle of the night in the dark."],[2149.39,"And so he keeps banging on the gate."],[2152.99,"And when they opened the door and saw him, they were astonished."],[2155.95,"But motioning to them with his hand to keep silent, because he just escaped from prison."],[2160.83,"Yeah. He declared to them that the Lord had brought him out of the out of the prison."],[2167.39,"And he said, Go tell these things to James and to the brethren."],[2171.31,"And he departed and went to another place."],[2174.83,"So obviously, this isn't the Saint James who was just killed by hair."],[2179.95,"This is Saint James, the brother of the Lord."],[2180.99,"the Who is serving as the first overseer, first bishop, of Jerusalem."],[2187.53,"So that's why he says, Go tell James that I'm free, but then you notice he goes somewhere else."],[2193.61,"Why? Well, because they're about to come looking for him."],[2195.85,"Yeah. And if they came looking for him and found him at that house, they probably kill everyone in that house for having helped him escape."],[2203.94,"So, not just for the sake of himself, but for the sake of the community, he he goes."],[2211.78,"Then as soon as it was day, there was no small stir among the soldiers about what had become of Peter."],[2218.34,"That's a nice understated translation."],[2222.5,"Among other reasons, because the penaltyy for dereliction of duty in the militar at this point in history was death."],[2224.74,"No small stir, yeah"],[2231.92,"So they're concerned that all of a sudden he's gone."],[2236.88,"But when Herod had searched for him and not found him, he examined the guards and commanded that they should be put to death."],[2243.85,"So he's angry."],[2245.3,"Because he calls them and questions them, and none of all of them claim to not know anything."],[2249.06,"Uh-huh. So he says, Well, that's it."],[2251.64,"Which to him sounds like a conspiracy amongst them."],[2255.26,"That you you guys are up to something, you're in on it, somebody bribed you to let him go."],[2259.9,"Something's going on here."],[2262.54,"And he went down from Judea to Caesarea and stayed there."],[2266.94,"Okay. So he leaves and goes to his palace in Caesarea"],[2267.86,"So he's just meh."],[2274.82,"Now Herod had been very angry with the people of Tyran Sidon."],[2278.66,"Okay, that's up in what's now Lebanon."],[2283.86,"But they came to him with one accord, and having made Blastus the king's personal aid their friend, they asked for peace because their country was supplied with food by the king's country."],[2294.9,"Remember, this famine is still going on."],[2297.3,"And so there'd been this rift right between the people up in Tyran Sidon."],[2303.64,"Up in what's now Lebanon and Herod."],[2306.5,"They hadn't been getting a law."],[2309.78,"That was outside the Tetrarchy."],[2311.54,"Uh-huh Yeah. But they had had poor relations."],[2315.66,"But there's this famine now."],[2318.19,"And sort of their best source of food up there in Lebanon is Herod."],[2325.39,"And so they decide they want to make nice."],[2328.51,"So they go to this Blasus, who is apparently Herod's friend."],[2332.73,"He's one of Herod's aides."],[2334.57,"And they make friends with him."],[2336.17,"They ingratiate themselves to him and they say, Hey, maybe you can go and talk to Herod and tell him we're not so bad."],[2343.37,"We want to be friends and make peace."],[2345.45,"We don't want anything out of it."],[2347.05,"Get us some food."],[2348.17,"But right. We'll we'll we'll sort this out."],[2354.17,"So on a set day, Herod. arrayed in royal apparel, sat on his throne and gave an oration to them"],[2363.17,"So basically he call he calls them in."],[2369.5,"Calls in the people from Tyran Sidon who had come to him to try to make peace."],[2374.06,"These are no, these are representatives."],[2376.16,"The people who have come to him to make peace."],[2378.08,"Calls them into his throne room."],[2379.7,"Puts on all his royal garb, sits at his throne, and he gives them this speech."],[2385.46,"Okay. Gives them this speech."],[2388.59,"And the people kept shouting the voice of a god and not of a man."],[2394.45,"So they're still probably trying to aggratiate themselves."],[2396.93,"Oh, you're a beautiful soldier."],[2398.21,"You speak like a god, not like a human being"],[2398.73,"This is this is typical Hellenistic flatter."],[2404.89,"You know, oh, how regal and majestic you are, Herod."],[2409.5,"Then immediately an angel of the Lord struck him because he did not give glory to God, and he was eaten by worms and died."],[2421.34,"So Herod doesn't get to execute those soldiers because God executes Herod."],[2426.78,"Uh-huh. Um the the the uh the interesting thing here is that you see where where we reached the the step too far."],[2441.51,"Remember uh when when Jesus in uh St"],[2446.51,"Mark's Gospel talks about the unforgivable sin."],[2450.01,"He says it's blasphemy against the against the Holy Spirit."],[2454.46,"So Herod isn't struck dead when he kills when he turns Jesus over to be killed."],[2460.86,"He's not struck dead when he kills Saint John the Forerunner, he's not struck dead when he kills Saint James, he's not struck dead when he tries to kill Saint Peter, but when he sits there and allows himself to be worshipped as a god."],[2473.18,"Uh-huh. That is the step too far."],[2480.17,"That's the point where no more time for repentance."],[2485.99,"And so it's at this point that he's eaten by worms and dies, which is a very unpleasant way to die."],[2492.95,"As we've already seen with St."],[2494.71,"Luke's description of how of how Judas died."],[2498.47,"He doesn't miss words about how these people get their comeuppance."],[2504.79,"But the word of God grew and multiplied."],[2507.51,"And Barnabas and Saul returned from Jerusalem when they had fulfilled their ministry, and they also took with them John whose surname was Mark."],[2517.03,"So much for Herod."],[2520.81,"And his attempts to what one of the themes we're seeing here in the book of Acts is that these people set out to attack Christ to attack his church."],[2531.86,"And it ends up, they end up destroying themselves."],[2536.34,"And the church ends up prospering at every turn."],[2560.74,"He's gonna show up here later on in the book of Acts."],[2564.18,"At Herod Agrippa."],[2565.7,"Uh-huh. There's a bunch of them."],[2572.78,"So um and then uh they the the Romans eventually sort of get tired of them and say, you're not really helping us keep the Jews under control because they keep revolting and you're causing trouble yourselves, so they end up getting rid of them too."],[2592.3,"But that's so okay."],[2597.1,"That's the end of a chapter, is a good place to stop, I think."],[2601.02,"So thank you, everybody."],[2604.86,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2612.22,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancient faith.com."],[2617.5,"That's whole.com.counsel at ancientfaith"]],"o":[{"t":21.36,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 11:27-28 - Prophets come to Antioch","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Prophets come from <b>Jerusalem to Antioch</b>; <b>Agabus</b> stands, shows by the Spirit a <b>great famine</b> coming</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Sort of out of the blue\" - sounds like <b>Old Testament</b> again</li><li class=\"d0\">Need to understand what <b>prophet</b> means</li><li class=\"d1\">modern use ≠ OT use</li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew <b><i>navi</i></b>; Greek <b><i>prophetes</i></b> → \"prophet\"</li><li class=\"d1\">we think = <b>predicts the future</b>; <b>not</b> what it meant</li><li class=\"d1\">some of it about future; some about <b>present</b>, some about <b>past</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Word used by <b>pagans</b> too - Near East <i>navi</i>, Greek</li><li class=\"d1\">false prophets in OT: <b>Balaam son of Beor</b>, prophet of a Canaanite god</li><li class=\"d0\">Agabus is a <b>prophet in the OT sense</b>, not a fortune-teller</li></ul>"},{"t":116.82,"lv":3,"h":"What a prophet was","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Prophet = <b>representative</b> - one <b>called by God</b> (or a god) with a <b>message for a particular purpose</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Went with a <b>lifestyle</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT <b>1-2 Kings (3-4 Kingdoms in LXX)</b>: whole <b>communities of prophets</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Elijah</b> = <i>sine qua non</i> of the prophets; <b>St. John the Baptist</b> in NT</li><li class=\"d0\">Called to the lifestyle and given the message</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul on the road to Damascus</b> (ch. 9): language drawn from <b>OT prophet call scenes</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Isaiah</b>: vision of God enthroned in the temple, sent with message</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jeremiah</b>: formed in mother's womb → \"prophet to the nations\" = <b>Gentiles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul in <b>Galatians</b>: called from mother's womb to be <b>apostle to the Gentiles</b> - crossover</li><li class=\"d0\">Prophets = people given a <b>commission to go and say/do something</b></li></ul>"},{"t":265.94,"lv":3,"h":"Prophets call people back to Torah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Prophets didn't preach just anything</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"<b>lucky lotto numbers</b> for next week\" or \"don't plant this side of the Jordan, it'll flood\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>specific</b> stuff, for a specific reason</li><li class=\"d0\">Primarily <b>repeating and calling the people back to the Torah</b> - teaching God had already revealed</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern: \"you are <b>disobedient</b>, doing what God forbade\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>repent</b> or judgment comes</li><li class=\"d1\">or judgment already came: \"<b>the reason it befell you</b> is X, Y, Z\"</li><li class=\"d1\">turn back and repent → <b>God will bless and restore</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Future-talk, but focus is <b>not just predicting</b> - it is \"what happens if you follow or turn back\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Source: end of <b>Deuteronomy 28-30</b> - \"today I set before you <b>life and death</b>, blessings and curses. <b>Choose</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">even: once thrown out of the land, if you turn back <b>I will still bless you</b> - \"he knew it was what was going to happen\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Core message always: \"you've been choosing death - <b>choose life</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":398.89,"lv":3,"h":"Prophetic word continues in preaching","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Phenomenon doesn't just stop</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Preaching ministry of the church</b> = continuation of the prophetic word</li><li class=\"d1\">why we call it a <b>homily</b> - \"almost the same\" word</li><li class=\"d1\">a homily should say <b>the same thing the Scriptures said</b>: \"come back to this\"</li><li class=\"d0\">These are <b>Jewish Christians</b> going to the <b>Jewish Christian community</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why their ministry understood in <b>prophetic terms</b> - Jewish context</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul and Barnabas</b> had been preaching to the <b>nascent Gentile Christian community</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Gentiles wouldn't have understood it the same way</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Agabus</b> has a message for that community - \"not the last we'll see of St. Agabus\"</li></ul>"},{"t":517.93,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 11:28 - The famine in Claudius' days","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Agabus: famine coming - and it <b>actually happened</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Also happened\" sounds confusing - not a second famine; the famine he spoke of happened <b>in the days of Claudius</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Few <b>temporal markers</b> in Acts</li><li class=\"d1\">Claudius → now in the <b>40s</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul's calling on the <b>road to Damascus ~35 AD</b> (\"conversion\" for simplicity)</li><li class=\"d0\">→ <b>considerable number of years</b> have passed</li></ul>"},{"t":593.85,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 11:29-30 - Relief sent to Judea","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Disciples, each <b>according to his ability</b>, send relief to the brethren in Judea - via <b>Barnabas and Saul</b> to the elders</li><li class=\"d0\">Because of the famine they take a <b>collection</b> → sent to <b>Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Important for several reasons</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Antioch Jewish community</b> large, established, <b>wealthier</b> than most Jews in Judea</li><li class=\"d1\">In Judea <b>70% of non-Roman land</b> owned by <b>high priests and their family</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>economic oppression</b> by Sadducees, chief priests, religious leaders - few of them follow Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">Jerusalem Christians not the landed class: <b>Peter, John</b> - fishermen, tradesmen</li><li class=\"d0\">So Antioch <b>shares</b> with the poorer community</li></ul>"},{"t":693.89,"lv":3,"h":"\"The brethren\" - one family, not congregationalists","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Notice: \"<b>the brethren in Judea</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Already in the <b>40s</b> - one <b>family across geographic distance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"a church here, a church there, we get along\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not congregationalists</b>: \"our group, we govern it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Helping each other <b>financially</b>; <b>teachers going back and forth</b>; one body spread out</li><li class=\"d0\">A <b>shift</b>: <b>synagogues</b> in all these places, but Jewish communities centered on the <b>Temple</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Temple = <b>sacrifices</b>, rituals, \"all the action\"</li><li class=\"d1\">synagogues = gathering places for those who can't get to Jerusalem - Rome, Cyrene, far away</li><li class=\"d0\">Churches don't view Jerusalem as \"the <b>King Church</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ</b> is with them in <b>Antioch</b> (Barnabas) and in <b>Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>Church of Christ</b> = one body spread out</li></ul>"},{"t":829.03,"lv":3,"h":"Against scholars: one church already","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why he presses it: scholars say <b>1-2 Timothy, Titus, Ephesians</b> can't be Paul's - they speak of \"<b>the church</b>\" as one big thing</li><li class=\"d1\">supposedly idea came <b>long after Paul was dead</b>; \"separate communities, all did things differently\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>here in Acts, in the 40s</b>, they already see themselves as <b>one family, one body</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Action = joint act of <b>Jewish Christians and Hellenist Christians</b>, bonding them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"one would hope\" - <b>tensions</b> still coming, here and especially in <b>Galatians</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sending collection with <b>Barnabas and Saul</b> = attempt to present a <b>united front</b></li><li class=\"d1\">also lets them tell Jerusalem the <b>wonderful things</b> in Antioch over the last year</li><li class=\"d0\">Close relationship - <b>one family</b>, not two geographic units</li><li class=\"d0\">Q&amp;A aside: \"shame of us\" - Jesus wants <b>one church</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Will return in <b>Galatians</b> - Paul works to avoid <b>a Gentile church and a Jewish church</b></li><li class=\"d1\">that would be a <b>betrayal of the gospel</b>: <b>Jesus is Lord of everyone</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tensions will still pull them apart over a few issues</li></ul>"},{"t":1034.43,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:1 - Herod stretches out his hand","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"About that time <b>Herod the king</b> stretched out his hand to harass some from the church\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not the same Herod - \"a couple of Herods\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Opening a bit past the chapter break; chapter 12 verse 1</li></ul>"},{"t":1043.47,"lv":3,"h":"Herod the Great and his son the tetrarch","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Herod the Great</b> - killed the <b>infants</b> at Jesus' birth (Matthew)</li><li class=\"d1\">not Jewish: <b>Idumean</b> = Edomite; \"by modern terminology, an <b>Arab</b>\"; desert tribe</li><li class=\"d1\">great politician - weaseled his way into being <b>king</b> via the Romans</li><li class=\"d1\">like the <b>queen of England</b>: little real power; official title <b>Ethnarch</b> = king of the people</li><li class=\"d1\">Romans cared about <b>land, resources, trade roads</b>, not the people - \"like the animals living there\"; useful as slave labor</li><li class=\"d1\">tried to <b>romance Cleopatra</b>; switched sides in the <b>Mark Antony / Octavian</b> civil war</li><li class=\"d1\">Romans unhappy when he died → <b>split territory in four</b>, one piece per son</li><li class=\"d1\">son = <b>Herod the Tetrarch</b> = \"ruler of a fourth\"</li><li class=\"d1\">father's legacy: <b>building projects</b> - the <b>Temple</b> worked on 40 years, baths, theaters, fortresses, palaces; \"a great artist\"</li><li class=\"d0\">This Herod = \"Herod the not so great\" - the one <b>Pilate sent Jesus to</b> (\"don't bother me\")</li><li class=\"d0\">Now causing trouble for the Jerusalem Christians</li></ul>"},{"t":1317.04,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:2 - James killed with the sword","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Then he killed <b>James, the brother of John</b>, with the sword\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>James the brother of the Lord</b> (Joseph's son) - he stays <b>leader of the Church of Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d0\">This = <b>James son of Zebedee</b>, St. John's brother</li><li class=\"d1\">Gospels' <b>inner circle: Peter, James, John</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>first apostle martyred</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Three Jameses</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>James the Great</b> = son of Zebedee</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>James the Lesser</b> = son of Alpheus, one of the Twelve</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>James the brother of the Lord</b> - not one of the Twelve</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Santiago? - <i>Iago</i> is Spanish form of James; guess = brother of the Lord, not sure</li><li class=\"d0\">Why so many: English <b>James</b> translates <b><i>Iakobos</i> = Jacob</b> - very common Jewish name</li></ul>"},{"t":1447.14,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:3-5 - Peter arrested","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Saw it <b>pleased the Jews</b> → proceeds to seize <b>Peter</b> too - during <b>Days of Unleavened Bread</b> (week before Passover)</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The Jews\" = <b>Jewish authorities of Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">already hostile; used <b>mob violence</b> (Stephen stoned) - no authority to execute</li><li class=\"d1\">Herod <b>can</b> execute - as with <b>John the Baptist</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Herod has <b>no real power</b> - only <b>popularity</b>: \"they're happy, I'll kill another one\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter delivered to <b>four squads of soldiers</b>, to be brought out <b>after Passover</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Herod not truly Jewish - \"faking it\"; must be sensitive - executing at Passover wouldn't go over well</li><li class=\"d0\">Four squads = locked in the <b>garrison</b>; \"secure as you can get\"</li><li class=\"d0\">→ would have to get past the whole garrison</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Constant prayer</b> offered to God for him by the church</li></ul>"},{"t":1606.68,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:6-11 - The angel frees Peter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Night before the trial: Peter <b>sleeping</b>, bound with <b>two chains between two soldiers</b>, guards at the door</li><li class=\"d1\">remember earlier arrest: Peter and John arrested, next thing out preaching again → Herod \"making very sure\"</li><li class=\"d1\">one arm chained to each soldier; two more at the door</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angel of the Lord</b> stands by him, <b>light shone</b>; strikes his side - \"Arise quickly\"; <b>chains fall off</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Gird yourself</b>, tie on your sandals... put on your garments, follow me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter thinks he is seeing a <b>vision</b>; passes <b>first and second guard posts</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Iron gate</b> to the city <b>opens of its own accord</b>, like the chains</li><li class=\"d0\">Down one street → <b>angel departs</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Peter \"comes to himself\": <b>\"Now I know for certain\"</b> the Lord sent his angel - from Herod and \"<b>the expectation of the Jewish people</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">what they expected = a <b>public execution</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1701.23,"lv":3,"h":"Girding up the loins","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Gird yourself</b>\" - King James: \"gird up your loins\"</li><li class=\"d0\">People wore <b>robes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">take the <b>base of the robe</b>, tuck it between the legs, into the <b>belt</b> = \"more like shorts\"</li><li class=\"d1\">lets you <b>move efficiently</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Angel is saying: \"come on, <b>get ready, let's go</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1815.77,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:12 - Mary, mother of John Mark","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Peter goes to the <b>house of Mary, mother of John whose surname was Mark</b> - many gathered <b>praying</b></li><li class=\"d0\">New person introduced</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Surname</b>\" is not a surname</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>John</b> = from Hebrew <b>Jonah</b> - common name</li><li class=\"d1\">real second name = <b>Marcus</b>, Latin Roman name</li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Saul → Paulos</b>: Jews doing business in the Roman world took <b>Greek or Latin names</b> - Romans couldn't pronounce Jewish names (<b><i>sh</i></b> sounds etc.)</li><li class=\"d1\">today: Asian friends say \"people call me <b>Peter</b>, <b>Mike</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if your name is Bulos, you go by Paul\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No last names then - <b>Marcus</b> = name used in business</li></ul>"},{"t":1955.55,"lv":3,"h":"Mary's house and John Mark","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Mary</b> from <b>Miriam</b>, Moses' sister - popular women's name</li><li class=\"d0\">Her having a <b>house</b> implies <b>money</b></li><li class=\"d1\">husband had the house in Jerusalem, died, left it to her</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Meeting place</b> for the Christian community there - probably one of the larger houses, a <b>well-to-do</b> member</li><li class=\"d1\">fits: <b>business with the larger world</b> → the Roman name</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>This is the St. Mark who wrote the gospel</b> - \"this is him\"</li><li class=\"d1\">will show up later: works with <b>Paul</b>, then with <b>Peter</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gospel records <b>Peter's preaching</b> - he was Peter's companion in <b>Rome</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still a <b>very young man</b> at this point</li></ul>"},{"t":2054.74,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:13-17 - Rhoda at the gate","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Peter heads to the house where they pray for his freedom</li><li class=\"d0\">Knocks at the gate; <b>Rhoda</b>, a <b>servant girl</b>, answers</li><li class=\"d0\">Recognizes his voice - <b>in gladness</b> doesn't open, runs in: \"Peter's at the door!\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They: \"<b>You are beside yourself</b>\" (\"nice translation\") = \"you're crazy, he's in prison, they execute him tomorrow\"</li><li class=\"d0\">She insists → \"<b>It is his angel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they think he's already been executed early, \"this is his spirit\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Meanwhile Peter <b>keeps knocking</b> in the dark</li><li class=\"d0\">They open and are <b>astonished</b>; he <b>motions for silence</b>, declares the Lord brought him out</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Go tell these things to James and to the brethren</b>\" - departs to <b>another place</b></li><li class=\"d1\">this James = <b>brother of the Lord</b>, first <b>overseer/bishop of Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why leave: they're coming to look for him → would <b>kill everyone in the house</b> → goes <b>for the community's sake</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2211.78,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:18-19 - Herod and the guards","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Morning: \"<b>no small stir</b> among the soldiers\" - \"nice understated translation\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>penalty for dereliction of duty = death</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Herod searches, doesn't find him; <b>examines the guards</b>, commands them <b>put to death</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all claim to know nothing → sounds like a <b>conspiracy</b>, \"somebody bribed you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Herod goes <b>down from Judea to Caesarea</b>, stays there - his palace</li></ul>"},{"t":2274.82,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:20-23 - Tyre and Sidon; Herod struck down","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Herod angry with people of <b>Tyre and Sidon</b> - up in what's now <b>Lebanon</b>, outside the tetrarchy</li><li class=\"d0\">They come <b>with one accord</b>, make <b>Blastus the king's aide</b> their friend, ask for <b>peace</b></li><li class=\"d1\">country supplied with food by the king's country - <b>famine still going on</b></li><li class=\"d1\">best food source is Herod → they <b>ingratiate themselves</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Set day</b>: Herod in <b>royal apparel</b> on his <b>throne</b> gives an <b>oration</b></li><li class=\"d0\">People shout: \"<b>the voice of a god and not of a man</b>\" - \"typical <b>Hellenistic flattery</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angel of the Lord struck him</b> - he did not give glory to God → <b>eaten by worms and died</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God executes Herod before he can execute the soldiers</li><li class=\"d1\">compare <b>Judas's death</b> in Luke's account - \"doesn't mince words\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Note the <b>step too far</b>: not struck for handing Jesus over, killing John, killing James, trying to kill Peter</li><li class=\"d1\">struck when he <b>lets himself be worshiped as a god</b></li><li class=\"d1\">recall Jesus in Mark: <b>unforgivable sin</b> = blasphemy against the Holy Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">\"no more time for repentance\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2504.79,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 12:24-25 - The word grew","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>word of God grew and multiplied</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Barnabas and Saul</b> return from Jerusalem, ministry fulfilled; take <b>John Mark</b> with them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"So much for Herod\" - theme of Acts: people set out to <b>attack Christ and his church</b> → <b>destroy themselves</b></li><li class=\"d1\">church <b>prospers at every turn</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2560.74,"lv":3,"h":"Herod Agrippa and end of chapter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">He'll <b>show up later in Acts</b> - <b>Herod Agrippa</b>; \"a bunch of them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Romans eventually tired of them - \"not helping keep the Jews under control\", they keep revolting and cause trouble → <b>got rid of them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">End of the chapter - good place to stop</li></ul>"}]});
